+# EQT v0.1 — quantitative quartic endpoint
+
+At zero offset epsilon=0, all finite-rank critical embeddings have an explicit sufficient radius R_star and quartic orbit-distance coercivity H-H_star >= (N/1600)d_g^4. For a target eta<=R_star, B_eta=N eta^4/1600 is a boundary barrier and delta_eta=eta^2 sqrt(N/(1600J)) is an all-time sufficient initial radius, J=max(a,25N). The zero-Gauss invariant subset is included.
+
+Two 192-bit Arb positive congruences and the frozen exact integer quartic replay pass. The manuscript supplies the intrinsic jet conversion and global fifth-order remainder absorption. Four exact rational budget examples pass. At a=N=1: R_star≈2.36008e-14, B_R≈1.93905e-58, delta_R≈2.78500e-30. These are conservative mathematical guarantees.
+
+Eight PDF pages visually checked. No empirical samples or new physical correspondence. Development, no registry entry; independent review pending; physical promotion 0. No sharp basin, attraction, endpoint forcing/model-error guarantee or infinite-rank flow is claimed.
